  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 128 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nCooler temperatures commence this weekend as surface high pressure \ncentered over the Southern Great Plains reinforces cooler air behind \nthe cold front. This yields afternoon highs in the upper 50s for \nmost, with low 60s expected in a few locations. From Sunday onward, \nreturn flow and mostly sunny skies bring a warming trend. At this \ntime, highs are forecast to reach the upper 70s to low 80s by the \nmiddle of next week. Low chances of rain (10-30%) return to the \nwestern half of the area Tuesday and Wednesday as shortwave \nimpulses move through southwest flow aloft. \n  \nGreening",
